sequenceDiagram
    actor A as AI Agent / LLM Application
    participant H as Agent Host / MCP Client
    participant R as Secured MCP Registry
    participant V as Trust & Verification Service
    participant P as Policy Enforcement Service
    participant X as Reflexive Core
    participant S as Secured MCP Server
    participant L as Provenance & Audit Service
    participant N as Alerts & Notifications

    A->>H: 1. Request an MCP capability
    H->>R: 2. Authenticate and discover MCP servers
    R->>V: 3. Verify publisher, version and attestation
    V-->>R: 4. Return verification status
    R->>P: 5. Evaluate access and usage policy
    P-->>R: 6. Return policy decision
    R->>X: 7. Request behavioral risk assessment
    X-->>R: 8. Return actor and server risk state
    R-->>H: 9. Return approved server configuration

    H->>S: 10. Invoke MCP capability
    S->>P: 11. Enforce runtime policy
    P->>X: 12. Submit execution context
    X->>X: 13. Analyze behavior and detect drift

    alt Normal behavior
        X-->>P: 14A. Permit execution
        P-->>S: 15A. Continue execution
        S-->>H: 16A. Return MCP result
        H-->>A: 17A. Deliver result
        S->>L: 18A. Record execution provenance
    else Elevated risk
        X-->>P: 14B. Require approval or restriction
        P-->>H: 15B. Return restricted response
        X->>L: 16B. Record anomaly and decision
        X->>N: 17B. Emit risk alert
    else Critical risk
        X-->>P: 14C. Block execution
        X->>R: 15C. Recommend suspension or revocation
        R->>V: 16C. Update security status
        X->>L: 17C. Record critical security event
        N-->>H: 18C. Notify client owner or administrator
    end
